**How to implement.** The experiment chart, the pop-out chart and Export data read the whole scan (the S9.1 brief: the Experiments bay, the experiment chart (`ExperimentChart.fs`, `chartForRun`) and the export path read v2; .spec-md §6: `Propagation.sampleMuellerSpun` and the run law are reused). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.1. In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: (1) `chartForRun` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:chartForRun`, as steps 252, 265, 266 and 289 left it) takes `(model)` and `(scan : Experiments.ExperimentScan)` in place of the chosen element, variable, capture, range, label and wavelength, and `chartForParams` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:chartForParams`), which nothing calls, is deleted. For each block with at least one axis, in order: its last axis is the x axis and its element the varied one whose captures (`model.captureDetectors`) and analyzer check (`noPolarizerOnPath`) apply as today; the x values are the axis's `sweptValues` (step 287), a `VaryR2` axis's range first clamped to [0, `Propagation.r2SweepMaxDegrees`] as today; and the points of its other axes (their product, first outermost) each give one group of series. Each path step is built once per block from the settings that touch it: a polarizer turns to a `VaryR1` setting on it, or to the physical angle of a `VaryDialReading` setting on it (step 289), else its R1; a sample takes its incidence from a `VaryR2` setting on it, its spin from a `VaryR1` or `VaryDialReading` setting on it, else its drawn incidence and R1; every element runs at a `VaryWaveLength` setting, else at `operatingWaveLength model scan.sourceWaveLengthOpt`; a step no setting of the block touches is built once (today's `FixedStep`), so a sample is re-solved only when something it depends on varies. Each group reads every captured branch as today, one series per branch and reading (`Intensity`, `Ψ`, `Δ`). A scan of one block of one axis gives exactly today's chart: series names, labels, title and description. Otherwise a series' name is today's name, then ` — ` and its group's settings as `<axis label>: <variable.label> <%g value><unit>` joined by `, `, then `, block <k>` when the scan has more than one block; the x label joins the distinct x-axis variables' labels with ` / `; `xAxisKind` is `AngularXAxis` when every x-axis variable is an angle (R1, R2, dial) and `NonAngularXAxis` otherwise; the title is today's title of the first block's x axis; and the description names the scan by `Experiment.description`'s block texts (step 288) in place of `varied element: …`. A block with no axis gives no series, and a scan of no series is the empty chart. (2) `model.experimentResult` charts `draft.scanOpt` with its last block read on `model.draftCapture`, empty when either is missing; `chartForExperiment` charts the experiment's scan, so step 288's one-axis limit goes; Export data (`exportDraftRun`, `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:exportDraftRun`) and the pop-out window read `experimentResult` as before (`ExperimentExport.fs:ExportedRun` unchanged), so the export carries every series. (3) `AGENTS.md`'s gotcha 'An experiment runs on the light's real path' says, in no more words, that an experiment's chart is its scan's: one series per value of the outer axes and captured branch, over the last axis of each block. No cache, option or other member is added. Tests (`ExperimentControlsTests`, ui-tests, over its table with a sample between a linear polarizer and two detectors, one on each branch): `a two-variable scan draws one series per value of its outer variable, read on each captured branch`: the draft of the sample's R2 over 20…60° (3 points), Add variable (`ExpAddScanAxis`), the sample's R1 over 0…90° (2 points), capture both, charts six intensity series, two per incidence (T and R), each over the x values 0 and 90, named `Intensity (T) — <sample label>: Incidence R2 20°` and so on, and each series' points equal the one-axis draft of R1 over 0…90° with the sample's incidence turned to that value, within 1e-12. `a collected multi-block experiment's chart holds every block's series`: a committed experiment of two blocks (the sample's R1 over 0…67.5° in 4 points read in T, then the block above) charts the first block's one series and the second block's six, the second's names ending `, block 2`. `the export of a two-variable draft carries every series of its chart` : Export data on the two-variable draft exports one run holding the chart's six series. `FsxAcceptanceTests` and `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests` pass as written: their one-axis numbers are unchanged.

**Acceptance.** After the chart reads the scan, `chartForRun` MUST draw every block of an `ExperimentScan`, one series per value of the outer axes and captured branch over the block's last axis, a one-axis scan giving today's chart exactly, and the draft chart, the collected chart and Export data MUST read it; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a two-variable scan draws one series per value of its outer variable, read on each captured branch`, `a collected multi-block experiment's chart holds every block's series` and `the export of a two-variable draft carries every series of its chart`, the count rising by 3, with `FsxAcceptanceTests` unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s29 invariants MUST pass.
